    "title": "Irondequoit Bay Outlet Bridge swings open for Summer boating - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Reagan Hillman ,\n11 hours ago\nROCHESTER, N.Y. (WROC) — The Irondequoit Bay Outlet Bridge will be closed to traffic until after Halloween 2026. It’s swung open to allow boaters to access Lake Ontario from the bay.\nThe bridge connects Lake Road in Webster to Culver Road in Irondequoit, and every year it swings open on April 1 so boats can use the channel during the summer months.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to RochesterFirst.",
    "summary": "ROCHESTER, N.Y. (WROC) — The Irondequoit Bay Outlet Bridge will be closed to traffic until after Halloween 2026. It’s swung open to allow boaters to access Lake Ontario from the bay. The bridge connects Lake Road in Webster to Culver Road in Irondequoit, and every year it swings open on April 1 so boats can use the channel during the summer months. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to RochesterFirst.",
